-- An over-budget `of` enumeration (21845 scene values, over the 10000 of
-- `defaultMaterializationCardinality`), so the materialization gate declines
-- dense enumeration and the plan-guided path must compile the body (task
-- plan-path-coverage-for-over-budget-bodies). Before that task the plan
-- traversal refused this body and the whole compile died.
--
-- ORACLE: the same program compiled densely with `--materializationBudget
-- 100000`, which agreed with every row below to a few ulps (summation order)
-- unless noted. numRed's own law at these logits: P(0) = 0.6704985969,
-- P(1) = 0.2900826155, P(2) = 0.0344722817, P(3) = 0.0044528186 (and
-- P(>= 2) = 0.0394187876, planEnumRecCountOfLazy).
--
-- Part 3 with the inner draw read twice. The scene is mentioned once but read
-- twice after substitution, so the value grouping must stay off (the two
-- copies share every leaf); counting syntactic occurrences alone enabled it and
-- answered 0.1202 at (1.0, 1.0). The oracle is numRed's own law on the
-- diagonal. Two readers means one world per scene path, a module too deep for
-- CPython's parser and Julia's (python-codegen-exceeds-parser-nesting-limit),
-- so this runs on the interpreter only, under `slow`; planMultiReaderInnerDraw
-- is its fast depth-3 twin on every backend.
data Color = Red | Green | Blue
data Object = NoObj | Obj color::Color
data Scene = Empty | SCons obj::Object, rest::Scene depth 7

neural readScene :: (Symbol -> Scene) of 7x.{Empty | SCons {NoObj | Obj {Red|Green|Blue}} x}

numRed s = if isEmpty s then 0.0 else (if isObj (obj s) then (if isRed (color (obj s)) then 1.0 else 0.0) else 0.0) + numRed (rest s)

main sym = draw scene = readScene sym in draw n = numRed scene in (n, n)
